mo></mrow><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\"><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">0</mn></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>, and find the limit of\nthis eigenvector as <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"\\varepsilon \\to\n0^{+}\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D700 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2192\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-msup space=\"4\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em;\"><mjx-TeXAtom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-TeXAtom></mjx-script></mjx-msup></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ε</mi><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>.</li>\n<li>Which conclusions of <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"thm-perron\">@thm-perron</span> survive the limit in these\ntwo examples, and which do not? Explain in one sentence why this is to\nbe expected.</li>\n</ol>\n</div>","file":"ch19-nonnegative/03-perron-frobenius.html"}